window.EN={"1":"The coup d'état that occurred in the royal capital Aquleia instantly spread like wildfire across all of Etruria.","2":"Cecilia, accompanying Princess Guinivere, escaped from the royal capital Aquleia.","3":"She went on to organize the anti-coup faction and fought battles across the land.","4":"But the coup faction, backed by the kingdom of Bern, held strong momentum.","5":"Furthermore, by the \"royal decree\" of King Mordred, whom they held in their grasp,","6":"two of the Three Generals—Douglas, the \"Great General,\" and Perceval, the \"Knight General\"—","7":"had also sided with the coup,","8":"and the anti-coup faction gradually began to be pushed back.","9":"Eventually, they were driven into an old castle at the western edge of the Missur Peninsula.","10":"Roy and the Lycian League army, having somehow managed to locate Cecilia and the others,","11":"left the Western Isles to rescue them and headed for the Missur Peninsula.","12":"Around that time, the anti-coup faction was holed up in the old castle,","13":"under attack from the combined forces of Bern and Etruria.","14":"Thanks to Cecilia's efforts, the anti-coup faction had continued to fight well, but","15":"by this point, their defeat was only a matter of time...","16":"Can you still not take the castle!?","17":"Y-yes... General Cecilia's resistance is stronger than we expected...","18":"That insolent woman... getting in my way again...!","19":"You seem to be having trouble, Narcian.","20":"......","21":"Y-your Majesty! When did you arrive...","22":"I just arrived a moment ago.","23":"It seems the Etrurian general is putting up quite a fight.","24":"Y-yes... I will take the castle swiftly...","25":"No need. I shall deal with her myself.","26":"Your Majesty, you needn't fight this yourself...","27":"It's fine. This will be good sport.","28":"Narcian, show me the way.","29":"What's the situation?","30":"It seems the castle hasn't fallen yet.","31":"I see! In any case, let's hurry!","32":"So, you're the \"Mage General,\" Cecilia?","33":"...King Zephiel of Bern.","34":"In light of how you've fought, I shall face you myself.","35":"......","36":"Ngh!!","37":"T-too strong...","38":"Did she faint? Hmph. How unimpressive.","39":"As expected of Your Majesty. Magnificent.","40":"So this is all an Etrurian general amounts to.","41":"Your Majesty, if it pleases you, might you leave this woman in my care?","42":"Hm?","43":"I bear this woman a bit of a grudge, and I'd like to make her thoroughly understand it...","44":"Hmph. Very well, do as you like.","45":"Much obliged. Hey, prepare the castle's dungeon for use.","46":"Yes, sir!","47":"The Bern army attacked the castle?","48":"Yes, sir.","49":"...That's not what we agreed.","50":"The arrangement was that we would handle Etruria's internal affairs ourselves.","51":"What should we do?","52":"...Was it General Narcian who commanded the attack on the castle?","53":"No, it's said to be King Zephiel himself.","54":"What? The king himself...","55":"In other words, Bern","56":"never intended to leave this to us in the first place.","57":"We will not move for the time being. Tell everyone so.","58":"Yes, sir!","59":"......","60":"Is it true that the castle has fallen?","61":"Yes... it seems we didn't make it in time.","62":"What happened to Cecilia?","63":"No word has come that she's been slain... but most likely—","64":"No, as long as there's a chance, I won't give up!","65":"Let's hurry to the castle!!","66":"Your Majesty! We've found Princess Guinivere.","67":"...I'll see her. Bring her here.","68":"Brother...","69":"Guinivere. It's been a while.","70":"Brother, why are you doing something like this...","71":"...dragging people who are living in peace into a war...","72":"\"Living in peace,\" you say? Hmph.","73":"Jealousy, envy, the thirst for power...","74":"In every nation, aren't people forever fighting over such petty things?","75":"Even if it washes blood with blood,","76":"can you call it peace just because it isn't outright war?","77":"T-that is...","78":"The world must be \"liberated\" from such petty things.","79":"My war is a war fought for that very purpose.","80":"But because of that, innocent people...","81":"Sacrifice is inevitable with change.","82":"That's not something limited to this matter alone.","83":"B-brother...","84":"Guinivere, you are my sister. My only living blood relative.","85":"Therefore, I will overlook this, just this once.","86":"But I will not forgive a second time. Understood? Remember that!","87":"......","88":"Narcian! There's the captain of Guinivere's personal guard in this army, isn't there?","89":"Yes, a dragon knight named Melady.","90":"Order her to send Guinivere back to the Bernese homeland.","91":"And see that the \"Fire Emblem\" is returned to the \"Shrine of Seals.\"","92":"Yes, sir.","93":"Brother...","94":"Melady...","95":"Lady Guinivere, I'm relieved more than anything that you're safe.","96":"Now then, let us head to Bern on my wyvern.","97":"...Lady Guinivere?","98":"Melady!","99":"W-what are you doing!? It's dangerous for you to hold a sword!","100":"Melady, please—let me go!","101":"!!","102":"If... if I were to let you go, what would you do from here?","103":"...I hear that Lord Roy of the Lycian League army has come nearby...","104":"What!? Are you saying you'd run to the enemy!?","105":"If things continue like this, the world...","106":"will be swallowed up by Bern... by my brother's army.","107":"No matter what reasoning he gives it, what my brother is doing now is rule by force.","108":"That something like that could lead anywhere good...","109":"I simply cannot believe it.","110":"......","111":"Please, Melady. Let me go... let me escape from here.","112":"...Just one thing.","113":"?","114":"There's one thing, just one, for which I resent you, Lady Guinivere.","115":"When you left Bern before, why didn't you consult with me, even just a word...","116":"T-that was out of consideration for your position, Melady...","117":"Did you think my loyalty to you was that shallow, Lady Guinivere?","118":"Before I am a knight of Bern, I am a knight of Princess Guinivere, the king's sister.","119":"That hasn't changed since the day I swore my knight's oath.","120":"Melady...","121":"So instead of pleading with me, if you'd simply commanded me, \"let me escape from here,\"","122":"I would gladly obey your order, Lady Guinivere.","123":"Melady, thank you...","124":"Please stop attacking! I'm not an enemy!","125":"What, not an enemy? Everyone, hold your attacks!","126":"L-Lord Roy, don't be taken in by the enemy's words...","127":"She might be an enemy envoy. Striking down an envoy would go against chivalry, wouldn't it?","128":"......","129":"Are you Lord Roy?","130":"...I am, but who are you?","131":"Lord Roy!","132":"P-Princess Guinivere, you're safe!","133":"Yes... with this woman's help, I managed to escape.","134":"I am called Melady. Please remember the name.","135":"Lord Roy, General Cecilia is alive.","136":"R-really?","137":"Yes. She suffered a deep wound, but she's now in the castle's dungeon...","138":"Understood. The details can wait... we need to hurry and rescue Cecilia!","139":"Are the preparations finished?","140":"Yes. Should you but give the order, the \"dragons\" are ready at any time...","141":"Narcian.","142":"I will lend you some of the \"dragons.\"","143":"Send part of the army toward the \"Nabata Desert.\"","144":"The \"Nabata Desert\"... that would be the region at the center of this peninsula, correct?","145":"That's right. It seems there's a \"hidden village\" there, dating back to the Scouring.","146":"Oh... then a \"divine weapon\" would be there as well...","147":"It's safe to assume so, almost certainly.","148":"It's of no use to us, but it would be troublesome if it fell into enemy hands.","149":"The unit I sent ahead has already begun its attack, but a shortage of forces is undeniable.","150":"Then I shall dispatch the \"dragons\" along with the mercenaries at once.","151":"Indeed.","152":"I'll leave with you a girl captured in the \"Nabata Desert.\"","153":"She's apparently a shaman living in the \"hidden village\" I mentioned. Get the details out of her.","154":"Understood. It's merely one \"hidden village,\"","155":"so I, Narcian, shall bring it down at once.","156":"...I'll remember those words.","157":"Yes, sir!","158":"Ngh... mmm... where am I... ugh","159":"Ah... your body is still... please don't move...","160":"Did you tend to this wound?","161":"...Yes... I'm not used to it, so I'm afraid I couldn't do it very well...","162":"No, you saved me. Thank you.","163":"More importantly, we need to escape from here quickly... ngh","164":"Ah... please don't move... your wound...","165":"We can't just stay like this...","166":"It's all right... the warm \"light\" that will save you... it's coming soon...","167":"Light?","168":"Yes... that \"light\" will be my salvation too...","169":"Let us wait... for the light's arrival...","170":"Just who... are you?","171":"I am... Sophia... the shrine maiden of... \"Nabata Village\"...","172":"What is this \"Nabata Village\"?","173":"Later... I'll tell you... in detail. For now... please... trust me...","174":"Did you call for me, Lord Perceval?","175":"We're withdrawing our troops from here.","176":"Huh? Are you certain?","177":"The action Bern took is clearly an insult to us.","178":"There's no reason for us to lend Bern any more of our strength.","179":"We'll return to the capital, Aquleia, once and discuss what comes next with Lord Douglas.","180":"Retreat at once!","181":"Yes, sir!","182":"Lord Narcian! They've appeared!","183":"T-the Lycian League army!!","184":"The Lycian League army, you say?","185":"Flaer! Didn't we finish them off at the Jutou governor's office!?","186":"Yes! N-no, well, we left the \"dragon\" behind, so—","187":"I can't believe... they survived...","188":"What did you say!?","189":"Then what of my position, as your superior officer!?","190":"If we can't finish off the Lycian League army as things stand, my competence itself will be doubted...","191":"I must do something about this somehow... still, to think they even brought down that \"dragon\"—","192":"...it seems they won't be dealt with so easily after all.","193":"L-Lord Narcian, what on earth should we... do...","194":"It can't be helped... Flaer.","195":"I will return to the Etrurian capital once, and work out a countermeasure against them there.","196":"You will remain here.","197":"What! M-me... alone?","198":"I won't say you need to defeat them. Just inflict as much damage as you can, and whittle down their forces.","199":"Lord Narcian! Are you... are you intending to make me a sacrifice!?","200":"Flaer... normally,","201":"the moment you failed to seize the Western Isles, your life would have been forfeit.","202":"I'm giving you a chance to make up for that failure.","203":"If anything, I'd like some gratitude. Heh heh heh...","204":"B-but...","205":"Or would you rather be executed by my own hand, right here, right now?","206":"I... understand...","207":"Well then, I'm counting on you. Heh heh heh...","208":"Perceval. It's been a while.","209":"...You're... it can't be...","210":"Have you forgotten my face?","211":"No, that's impossible. The prince... passed away.","212":"...It's only natural that you can't believe it.","213":"After all, here I stand, when I should be dead.","214":"Prince Mildain!","215":"You were alive...? Truly...","216":"I've caused you worry for a long time.","217":"...It's been over a year since the time I was assassinated, hasn't it?","218":"Assassinated!? You... it was a fall from your horse...","219":"No, I was struck by a poisoned arrow while on horseback.","220":"First the horse was struck... and then, as I fell from the horse that had bolted, once more—","221":"Good heavens...","222":"Douglas realized what had happened immediately and had me declared dead as I was.","223":"A different body was placed in the coffin,","224":"and he made it appear as though everything had gone exactly as the assassins intended.","225":"Then he entrusted me to his foster child, who got me safely away to the Western Isles...","226":"Lord Douglas...","227":"Even after arriving in the west,","228":"the poison's effects kept me in high fever, and for a long time I wandered the border between life and death.","229":"Douglas's foster child, caring for me in that state,","230":"apparently despaired many times, thinking I could no longer be saved.","231":"......","232":"The ones who saved me there were the resistance fighters of that land.","233":"It's ironic—without knowing it,","234":"they had gone and saved the very prince of Etruria they so despised...","235":"......","236":"Under their care, little by little, I recovered.","237":"And at the same time, what gradually came into view was","238":"the countless, egregious acts of cruelty committed by Etrurian nobles in the west...","239":"I was ashamed of my foolish former self, who had only ever had eyes for the homeland.","240":"My prince...","241":"While helping the resistance's activities on the island, I waited for a chance to return to my homeland.","242":"And then... I met Lord Roy,","243":"and seized that opportunity—at last... at last, I've made it back this far.","244":"My prince... I'm so glad you returned alive.","245":"For now, I'll keep my true identity hidden, but I'm with the Lycian League army.","246":"If you would pledge to me the same loyalty as before, unchanged...","247":"Please, give me your command.","248":"The only lord to whom I've dedicated my sword is you, and you alone, Prince Mildain.","249":"Lord Perceval~! It is you, right~?","250":"Oh good, I've been looking for you~. See, I'm—","251":"Wah, hey! Wait a second!! Stop your horse and listen to me!","252":"...Who are you?","253":"I'm shocked... we've met a few times before!","254":"...I feel like I've seen you at Lord Douglas's mansion.","255":"Yes! That's it, that's it! See, you do know me after all!","256":"The girl I met there was a bit more... ordinary.","257":"What? What's that supposed to mean!?","258":"Well, never mind. More importantly—","259":"I'm Larum! I've come as a messenger for Prince Mildain.","260":"Prince Mildain... you say?","261":"Don't talk nonsense. The prince died in an accident a year ago.","262":"Hee hee hee...","263":"Ta-dah! Can't you see this crest!?","264":"...That's... the prince's...!","265":"Heh. Looks like you're impressed.","266":"Now look at this letter too! The prince said it's for you, Lord Perceval!","267":"...... ...... ......","268":"This is... indeed the prince's handwriting.","269":"I see... so he really was alive... then there's no more room for hesitation!","270":"If the prince is with the Lycian League, then there is only one path for me to take.","271":"Huh? Already?","272":"Mmm... and I had more stuff prepared too~","273":"I was planning to say something cool, like \"If you'll still fight, then cut me down instead!\"~","274":"I brought this along, thinking you all could make use of it.","275":"If you use this ring, your build improves remarkably.","276":"...though I wouldn't really recommend it for women...","277":"Ah, this sword?","278":"I got it to protect myself when I heard the army was attacking, but","279":"it seems I just can't handle it.","280":"It's a pretty good sword, isn't it?","281":"I hear it belonged to some spirited boy who was fighting against Bern, just like you all.","282":"I'll give it to you, so please end this war quickly.","283":"Lady Cecilia, Lord Perceval, and Lord Douglas!","284":"These three are Etruria's strongest, the Three Generals.","285":"They wouldn't lose even to Bern's Three Dragon Generals... never.","286":"Lady Cecilia, in just a single blow...","287":"That... that was...","288":"That was King Zephiel of Bern...","289":"They say that Lord Perceval, the \"Knight General,\"","290":"is even now still pledging his loyalty to the late Prince Mildain.","291":"Isn't that lovely~","292":"Ngh, damn it... but still!","293":"I, too, am a wyvern knight of Bern—I'll show you my resolve!!","294":"Ngh... remember this—there are plenty of generals greater than me.","295":"Bern's army, the strongest on the continent, will not let you live...","296":"Cecilia!","297":"Roy... I showed you quite an unseemly sight, didn't I.","298":"What are you saying! I'm just truly glad you're safe.","299":"But that wound... are you all right?","300":"Yes, because this girl here tended to it for me.","301":"...And you are?","302":"I am called... Sophia... I'm the shrine maiden of... \"Nabata Village\"...","303":"She foretold that you would come, Roy.","304":"Come to think of it, she said she'd tell us the details...","305":"Yes... our village... ...is located to the east, in the Nabata Desert...","306":"There, we have... as much as possible... tried not to associate with the outside world...","307":"But... the kingdom of Bern... came to know of us...","308":"And they attacked?","309":"Yes... I was too slow to escape...","310":"I see... but why would Bern go after your village?","311":"I don't know...","312":"But perhaps... they learned of the \"dragon\" that lives in our village...","313":"A \"dragon,\" you say!?","314":"Yes... long, long ago, our village...","315":"was founded by \"dragons\" and \"humans\" joining hands together...","316":"...Something like that exists...","317":"...Lord Roy... I beg you...","318":"Please... save our village...","319":"But to be told that all of a sudden... it's rather hard to believe, you know.","320":"......","321":"...Either way,","322":"it's a fact that her village is being attacked by Bern, isn't it?","323":"Then let's go help them. We owe her a debt too, for saving Cecilia.","324":"...Thank you.","325":"So, if it's all right with you,","326":"could you tell us more about \"Nabata Village\" and the \"dragons\"?","327":"...If it's something I know... I'd be glad to...","328":"[Only triggers if every member of the NPC Knight General squad is still alive]","329":"General Perceval.","330":"Until further orders, we will remain stationed at this castle, prepared for an attack by the coup faction.","331":"I'm counting on you.","332":"This is a treasure we found within the castle. Please accept it.","333":"Then, General... Etruria... we leave it in your hands, please.","334":"I understand. Leave it to me.","335":"Yes, sir!"};
